  "secondary_categories": [],
  "slug": "sequences-promoter-38cf",
  "summary": "Four reports supply curated complex sets, pocket-diverse target selection, and ensemble-based screening, all aimed at structurally grounded ligand modeling.",
  "synthesis": "The items converge on structural resources for protein-ligand modeling, emphasizing controlled and diverse inputs. DockBind provides 18,332 quality-controlled docked complexes across 612 targets paired with affinity data for ML training and benchmarking. Ternary-PDB curates 76,702 PDB ternary structures and accompanies DiffTernary, a diffusion-based docking method for molecular glue ternary complexes. PocketVec descriptors map 51,535 druggable human pockets to select diverse targets for Target 2035 ligand dataset generation. ANTIOCH-VS is a modular open-source pipeline from sequence to ranked hits, combining ColabFold subsampling, AF2RAVE MD ensembles, docking and consensus ranking. The summaries give no comparative accuracy results, so the new contribution lies in dataset construction, target selection and workflow integration rather than demonstrated performance gains.",
